WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.310
Theatre is all about choices.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.460
What you share, what you hide.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:37.630
The same story, even the same lines can be
delivered a million ways.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.500
Those choices change everything.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.260
When I saw my first play, I fell in love.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.650
My choice for my life was made.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.600
Wist that goes with me.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.050
I was the lead in every school play. I was
the best young actress in the Midwest,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:02.310
according to an article in the Clayton
Chronicle where my dad was the editor.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.940
But a visiting director from New York agreed.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.820
After graduation, I'd go to Broadway.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.620
It was all so clear until, it wasn't.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:31.560
Acting is all about choices, and I had to
make one.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:48.580
There was a couple in town who couldn't
conceive and I thought it was best for everyone.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.050
There was no instant

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:55.240
success when I got to New York. No delayed
success either.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:01.480
I began to wonder if I was being punished for
my choice.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.550
The family sent me an update.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.860
They finally got pregnant.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:13.480
A miracle. And just like that, you had a baby
brother. You wouldn't be alone.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:21.100
I followed you from afar. I made a book about you, which
I cherish, but it also made me sad because I

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.200
thought I'd never see you again.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.890
But then there it was, a sign.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.250
A chance to finally meet you.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.530
Loretta Durkin. You still there?

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.230
Yes. Yes.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:36.390
Hi.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:42.450
Oh, hi. I'm so sorry. My agent assured me
that I was on the list.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.220
There you were.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.710
This is my manager, Dickie.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.990
He's not just my manager. He's also my
brother.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.870
My baby boy.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.400
So, darling.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.670
My darling.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.920
These last few months getting to know you,

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:06.170
they have been a dream. But I've been lying
to you.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:21.690
So why am I telling you this today? Because
it's time.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.020
And it's our sitzprobe rehearsal.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:45.620
Sitzprobe when the actors first perform with
an orchestra and you learn if all your

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:51.680
choices have produced something harmonious or
horrific.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:08.500
And... if there's still time to make it all
right.

